  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set that traces this failure end-to-end:\n\n1. **`pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`** \u2014 registers the `\"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\"` PostStartHook and generates the exact error `\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\"` when the repair loops don't succeed within 1 minute. Also selects between the legacy bitmap repair controller and the new `RepairIPAddress` controller based on the `MultiCIDRServiceAllocator` feature gate.\n2. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go`** \u2014 the `RepairIPAddress` controller (new since 1.27+, default path in 1.31+/1.33) that reconciles Service ClusterIPs against `IPAddress` objects; waits for the default ServiceCIDR before running its first sync.\n3. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/cidrallocator.go`** \u2014 `MetaAllocator`, which tracks per-`ServiceCIDR` allocators and only serves allocation requests once a CIDR's `Ready` condition is true \u2014 this is the readiness gate that produces `ipaddresses.networking.k8s.io \"<ip>\" is forbidden: not yet ready to handle request` style failures during the mixed-version window.\n4. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/ipallocator.go`** and **`interfaces.go`** \u2014 the per-CIDR `Allocator` with its `ready` atomic flag and `ErrNotReady`.\n5. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repair.go`** \u2014 legacy bitmap-based repair controller (pre-`MultiCIDRServiceAllocator`), relevant to the mixed-version race since old and new nodes run different repair logic simultaneously.\n6. **`pkg/controlplane/instance.go`** / **`pkg/controlplane/apiserver/server.go`** \u2014 wire the repair interval, feature gate, default-ServiceCIDR PostStartHook, and the `storage-readiness` PostStartHook into the apiserver.\n7. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/storage_readiness_hook.go`**, **`healthz.go`**, **`healthz/healthz.go`**, **`genericapiserver.go`** \u2014 the generic apiserver machinery: PostStartHook \u2192 readyz check (`informer-sync`, `poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers`) wiring, and the storage-readiness registration path.\n8. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/registry/generic/registry/store.go`** / **`rest.go`** \u2014 `StorageWithReadiness` interface implemented by the generic REST `Store`.\n\nTogether these explain the race: during a rolling upgrade, a v1.33 apiserver's `RepairIPAddress` controller waits on the `ServiceCIDR`/`IPAddress` informers and the default ServiceCIDR object to exist and be `Ready` before its first successful sync; if that doesn't complete within the apiserver's 1-minute PostStartHook window (contended by concurrent v1.32 apiservers still using the legacy bitmap allocator against the same etcd), `start-service-ip-repair-controllers` returns the \"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\" error, which fails the `poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers` readyz check and takes the node out of rotation until all nodes have converged on v1.33.",
